  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Friday)\nIssued at 217 AM CDT Sat Aug 29 2026\n\nThe hot and dry conditions will continue into next week with no \nevidence of any impactful synoptic-scale pattern change through \nthe end of the week. The subtropical ridge will continue to be the\nprimary influence of weather across the Southern Plains with \nagreement among deterministic and ensemble NWP. \n\nThe probabilistic National Blend of Models (NBM) forecast has \nvery little spread among the 10th and 90th percentile temperature \nforecast with even the 10th percentile several degrees above- \nnormal. As a result, there is a high confidence that above-normal \ntemperatures in the upper 90s to mid 100s deg F will persist all \nof next week. Bottom line--expect a heatwave next week.\n\nDrought conditions will worsen with the subtropical ridge \nblocking any weather systems that would bring rainfall across \nOklahoma and western north Texas. Therefore, elevated fire weather\nconditions will continue along with very dry fuels. The total \nfire environment will continue to be susceptible to initial attack\nfires to low-end large fires.\n\nMahale",
